# p_a7c3 — Both drive, weekend cycling, laptop at the office desk (fork of p_4e91)

The parent placed Yuki's laptop at entry_hook_e1 as its default resting spot, with only a "sometimes" block at desk_b1 on weekend evenings. The evidence against p_b2c8 (six looks at entry_hook_e1 in the 18–22 h weekday window finding no laptop) suggests the laptop is not left at the entry hook in the evening. This fork moves the laptop's weekday-evening home to desk_o1 (the office desk), where Yuki does her evening work and email. The office desk is a dedicated workspace; the bedroom desk (desk_b1) is for journaling and reading. Yuki arrives 17:30, puts the laptop on desk_o1, works until about 20:00, then the laptop stays there overnight. The notebook also goes to desk_o1 in the evening. The rest of the parent stays: no weekday cycling, weekend cycling 10–13, Omar's tablet at chair_k1, all work items out of house 8–17:30, Omar's helmet and bike lock out during his shift 13:40–23:00. What sets this apart from p_3f7a: at 20:00 on a weekday, the laptop is at desk_o1, not desk_b1. What would refute it: laptop_yuki sighted at desk_b1 on a weekday between 18:00 and 22:00, or at entry_hook_e1 in that window.

